+/* Card data, not code: the china_v2 card definition matched to the
+   hardware actually fitted on this board (Wileyfox Swift / Longcheer
+   L8150).
+
+   The 5 physical devices removed below are not present on this board:
+     1. A live RFFE bus scan (USID 1..15, channel 0..4) only finds
+        WTR4905, QFE2101 and QFE2340; channels 1-3 are empty and channel 0
+        mixes present and absent devices, so the bus itself works and this
+        is a genuine absence, not a read failure.
+     2. Visual inspection of the board: QFE2340 is fitted, QFE3320 is not.
+     3. The real OEM firmware for this same phone reads the same hw_id=151
+        (NV rf_hw_config) and its card-151 device list has exactly these
+        3 devices plus the terminator (checked byte for byte: all 4
+        "china" family cards sit at the same relative offsets in both
+        images, and the one that hw_id=151 dispatches to lists WTR4905,
+        QFE2101, QFE2340, TERMINATOR).
+
+   The December 2014 SDK tree this image is built from still has an older
+   card-151 definition, for a board revision that carries the ASM and
+   tuner devices removed here. With the old definition,
+   create_cmn_rf_devices() marks them RFC_DEVICE_MISSING_FATAL, so
+   rfc_set_card() fails and rfm_enter_mode() never brings up the radio at
+   all. Matching the card's own device list to reality (as the real OEM
+   firmware already does) fixes this at the source, rather than relaxing
+   the missing-device check in the RFC framework shared by every card. */
+#if 0  /* physically absent on this board */
   { /*Device: QFE3320_EPT */ 
     QFE3320, /* PHY_DEVICE_NAME */ 
     3, /* PHY_DEVICE_INSTANCE */ 
@@ -195,6 +221,7 @@
     FALSE, /* INIT */ 
     RFC_INVALID_PARAM, /* ASSOCIATED_DAC */ 
   }, /* END - Device: QFE3320_LB */ 
+#endif
 
